[I] Encoding detector library ported from Mozilla

[T] uchardet is an encoding detector library that takes a sequence of bytes
[T] in an unknown character encoding and attempts to determine the encoding
[T] of the text. It started as a C binding of Mozilla's universal charset
[T] detector and now detects more charsets more reliably, with a uchardet
[T] command line tool.

[U] https://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Software/uchardet

[A] Uchardet Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

